<title>USA: Standard Pacific ceo, ex-prez sell shares.</title>
<headline>Standard Pacific ceo, ex-prez sell shares.</headline>
<dateline>COSTA MESA, Calif 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard Pacific Corp chairman and chief executive Arthur Svendsen said he and Ronald Foell, former president and a director, completed the sale of 200,000 Standard Pacific common shares.</p>
<p>Svendsen said the sales were made for 1996 year-end tax reasons to offset significant capital gains arising out of a personal commercial real estate transaction unrelated to the Company.</p>
